 ### Polling Intervals
 
-The component supports configurable polling intervals to balance responsiveness and battery life:
+The component supports configurable polling intervals to balance responsiveness and battery life.
+All four intervals accept floats down to **0.2 s** (e.g. `3`, `2.5`, `0.2` are all valid):
 
 ```yaml
 tesla_ble_vehicle:
   # ... other configuration ...
   
-  # Polling intervals (in seconds)
-  vcsec_poll_interval: 10                      # Vehicle status polling (default: 10s, range: 5-300s)
-  infotainment_poll_interval_awake: 30         # Data polling when awake (default: 30s, range: 10-600s)
-  infotainment_poll_interval_active: 10        # Data polling when active (default: 10s, range: 5-120s)
-  infotainment_sleep_timeout: 660              # Wake window duration (default: 11min, range: 1-60min)
+  # Polling intervals (in seconds, floats allowed, minimum 0.2)
+  vcsec_poll_interval: 10                      # Vehicle status polling (default: 10s, range: 0.2-300s)
+  infotainment_poll_interval_awake: 30         # Data polling when awake (default: 30s, range: 0.2-600s)
+  infotainment_poll_interval_active: 10        # Data polling when active (default: 10s, range: 0.2-120s)
+  infotainment_sleep_timeout: 660              # Wake window duration (default: 11min, range: 0.2-3600s)
 ```
 
+
+> [!NOTE]
+> The upstream `yoziru/esphome-tesla-ble` library restricts `vcsec_poll_interval` to
+> integer values >= 5 (`cv.int_range(min=5)`), which rejects configurations such as
+> `vcsec_poll_interval: 3` with `value must be at least 5`. This fork lifts that
+> limit to 0.2 s so aggressive polling (e.g. `3` or even `0.2`) validates and works.
+> `vcsec_poll_interval` also drives the ESPHome `update_interval` of the hub component.
+
 **Polling Types:**
 - **VCSEC**: Basic vehicle status (sleep/awake, locked/unlocked, user presence) - safe to poll when asleep
 - **Infotainment Awake**: Detailed data (battery, charging state) when awake but not active
 - **Infotainment Active**: Frequent updates when charging, unlocked, or user present
 
 
+### Entity Declaration Styles (both are supported)
+
+Every auto-created entity can be exposed to Home Assistant with a custom id/name in
+one of two fully equivalent ways:
+
+**Style 1 - direct sub-keys of the `tesla_ble_vehicle:` block** (used by `packages/client.yml`):
+
+```yaml
+tesla_ble_vehicle:
+  id: tesla_ble_vehicle_id
+  # ...
+  locked:
+    id: vehicle_locked
+    name: "Tesla Vehicle Locked State"
+  user_present:
+    id: vehicle_user_present
+    name: "Tesla User Presence"
+  shift_state:
+    id: vehicle_shift_state
+    name: "Tesla Shift State"
+```
+
+**Style 2 - standard ESPHome platform blocks**:
+
+```yaml
+binary_sensor:
+  - platform: tesla_ble_vehicle
+    tesla_ble_vehicle_id: tesla_ble_vehicle_id
+    locked:
+      id: vehicle_locked
+      name: "Tesla Vehicle Locked State"
+    user_present:
+      id: vehicle_user_present
+      name: "Tesla User Presence"
+
+text_sensor:
+  - platform: tesla_ble_vehicle
+    tesla_ble_vehicle_id: tesla_ble_vehicle_id
+    shift_state:
+      id: vehicle_shift_state
+      name: "Tesla Shift State"
+
+sensor:
+  - platform: tesla_ble_vehicle
+    tesla_ble_vehicle_id: tesla_ble_vehicle_id
+    odometer:
+      id: vehicle_odometer
+      name: "Tesla Odometer"
+```
+
+Notes:
+- Declaring the *same* key in both places is rejected at config validation time
+  with a clear error message - pick one style per entity.
+- Removing a declaration does not delete the entity from the firmware: the
+  auto-created entity still exists internally and keeps receiving updates, but it
+  is `internal` and therefore not exposed to Home Assistant, and its custom `id:`
+  is gone (lambdas referencing that id will fail to compile).
+- Available binary_sensor keys: `asleep`, `user_present`, `locked`, `charging`,
+  `charge_flap_open`, `boot_open`, `frunk_open`, `windows_state`, `climate_on`,
+  `parking_brake`, `door_*`, `window_*`, `sunroof`.
+- Available sensor keys: `battery_level`, `range`, `range_rated_api`, `inside_temp`,
+  `outside_temp`, `driver_temp_setting`, `passenger_temp_setting`, `odometer`, `speed`,
+  `charger_power`, `charger_voltage`, `charger_current`, `charging_rate`, `charge_rate`,
+  `charge_energy_added` (alias: `energy_added`), `time_to_full_charge` (alias: `time_to_full`),
+  `tpms_*`, `max_soc`, `max_amps`, `charge_distance_added`, `charger_phases`,
+  `ble_disconnected_time`.
+- Available text_sensor keys: `shift_state`, `charging_state`, `iec61851_state`,
+  `defrost_state`, `charge_port_latch_state`.
+
 **IEC 61851 text sensor**
 
